\f1\b\fs34 \cf0 4. Epistemic classification\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa240\partightenfactor0

\f0\b0\fs30 \cf0 Classify each atomic claim into exactly one category:\
CONFIRMED_FACT:\uc0\u8232 Directly supported by reliable evidence sufficient to establish the narrowly stated fact.\
ATTRIBUTED_ALLEGATION:\uc0\u8232 A statement attributed to a source but not independently established.\
TECHNICAL_UNCERTAINTY:\uc0\u8232 An unresolved question about technical behavior, system architecture, capability, or mechanism.\
DISPUTED_FACT:\uc0\u8232 A factual assertion for which supplied evidence contains materially conflicting accounts.\
Also provide verification_status separately:\
VERIFIED, PARTIALLY_VERIFIED, UNVERIFIED, CONTESTED, or NOT_ASSESSABLE.\
Confidence is not the same as verification status.\
An accurately quoted allegation may have high attribution confidence while its underlying factual truth remains unverified.\
\pard\pardeftab720\sa280\partightenfactor0

