Step 6: Analyze causal relationships, alternatives, and limitations.\
Step 7: Identify material uncertainty and disagreements.\
Step 8: Derive organizational risk and control implications.\
Step 9: Prepare decision-maker and consultant guidance.\
Step 10: Perform an evidence-consistency audit.\
